{"columns":["notice_id","section_id","field_id","ordinal","value"],"row_count":45,"rows":[[46778882,"1","BT-21-Lot",0,"General Waste"],[46778882,"1","BT-24-Lot",0,"Lot 1 - General Waste\nProvision of a daily collection and treatment service for:\n•\tResidual waste (known as general waste to the organisation)\n•\tDry mixed recycling (Plastic, Paper, Cardboard, Tins & Cans)\n•\tProvision of a collection and treatment service at intervals appropriate to the type of wast"],[46778882,"2","BT-21-Lot",0,"Hazardous; Chemical and Clinical Waste"],[46778882,"2","BT-24-Lot",0,"Provision of a collection and treatment service at intervals appropriate to the type of waste for:\n•\tBiohazardous material\n•\tSolvent waste halogenated and non-halogenated\n•\tClinical waste"],[46778882,"ORG-GB-COH-530008893","BT-500-Organization-Company",0,"VEOLIA ES (UK) LIMITED"],[46778882,"ORG-GB-FTS-4485","BT-500-Organization-Company",0,"Sheffield Hallam University"],[46778882,"ORG-GB-UKPRN-10007157","BT-500-Organization-Company",0,"Sheffield Hallam University"],[46778882,"PROCEDURE","BT-21-Procedure",0,"Waste Management Service"],[46778882,"PROCEDURE","BT-24-Procedure",0,"Sheffield Hallam University disposes of approximately 800 tonnes of waste each year, making waste management one of the University's most significant environmental impacts.\nEffective waste management is a core commitment within the University's Environmental Policy.\nThe awarded contract supports the"],[46788427,"1","BT-24-Lot",0,"Contract to provide mental health in school teams. This notice shows as the intention to award a contract to an existing provider following PSR Direct Award C from 01/07/2025 to 31/03/2028. The estimated total value of this contract is £18,278,310.10"],[46788427,"ORG-GB-CHC-Registered charity number 518048","BT-500-Organization-Company",0,"Compass"],[46788427,"ORG-GB-FTS-123665","BT-500-Organization-Company",0,"BSMHFT"],[46788427,"ORG-GB-FTS-140442","BT-500-Organization-Company",0,"BIRMINGHAM & SOLIHULL MENTAL HEALTH NHS FOUNDATION TRUST"],[46788427,"PROCEDURE","BT-21-Procedure",0,"Provision of mental health school teams"],[46788427,"PROCEDURE","BT-24-Procedure",0,"The provision of mental health in schools teams across Birmingham, waves 9, 10, 12, 13 and 14."],[46800200,"ORG-GB-MPR-IP21180R","BT-500-Organization-Company",0,"Cadarn Housing Group (AA58745)"],[46800200,"PROCEDURE","BT-21-Procedure",0,"Procurement of Pest Control Services — Cadarn Housing Group (PRO 023)"],[46800200,"PROCEDURE","BT-24-Procedure",0,"Cadarn Housing Group, on behalf of Cadwyn Housing Association Limited and Newydd Housing Association (1974) Limited, invites tenders for the provision of reactive pest control services across its residential housing portfolio in South and Mid Wales.\nThe successful contractor will be required to deli"],[46805334,"1","BT-24-Lot",0,"Contract relating to the provision of mental health school teams, in Birmingham, for Waves 13 and 14. This notice is confirmation of an award having been made due to an urgent circumstance (this is an urgent award) with an estimated lifetime value of circa £1,300,000 commencing 1 April 2026 to 31 Ma"],[46805334,"ORG-GB-CHC-Registered charity number 518048","BT-500-Organization-Company",0,"Compass"],[46805334,"ORG-GB-FTS-123665","BT-500-Organization-Company",0,"BSMHFT"],[46805334,"ORG-GB-FTS-140442","BT-500-Organization-Company",0,"BIRMINGHAM & SOLIHULL MENTAL HEALTH NHS FOUNDATION TRUST"],[46805334,"PROCEDURE","BT-21-Procedure",0,"Provision of Mental Health School Teams"],[46805334,"PROCEDURE","BT-24-Procedure",0,"Provision of mental health school team service in Birmingham, relating to Waves 13 and 14"],[46923980,"1","BT-24-Lot",0,"Bristol, North Somerset and South Gloucestershire Integrated Care Board (BNSSG ICB) is extending a number of current Community Mental Health Supporting Services contracts by 1-2 years.  This is being undertaken in order to align the services to the emerging BNSSG Community Mental Health Programme (C